Lutyens Delhi/Jantar Mantar 

Abhijeet Dipke Says He Will Serve Tea to Delhi Police

 Alleged ta vendor Was Stopped by police from serving tea to protestors 

 CJP leader Abhijeet Dipke alleged that Delhi Police stopped a young tea vendor from serving tea to protesters at Jantar Mantar. 

"Tomorrow, I will personally distribute tea to Delhi Police personnel. Selling tea is not a crime. Show a big heart. And who knows, what if a tea seller becomes Prime Minister again?" he said.

 #Delhi #JantarMantar #Protest
@abhijeet_dipke @cockroachisback
@DelhiPolice 
@CPDelhi

Major Highlights of the Day:

🔹 03 alleged members of the Prince Teotia Gang were arrested after an exchange of fire in the Saket extortion firing case by teams of @DCPSouthDelhi.

🔹 @CrimeBranchDP arrested the wife of an alleged extortion syndicate kingpin for laundering proceeds of crime & concealing illegally acquired assets

🔹 03 alleged sharpshooters, including a CCL linked to the Himanshu Bhau Gang, apprehended by the team of @dcp_outernorth & illegal firearms with live cartridges recovered

🔹Delhi Police facilitated permission & ensured peaceful conduct of the CJP protest at Jantar Mantar through robust security arrangements. During the protest at Jantar Mantar, Delhi Police safeguarded & facilitated the return of several misplaced mobile phones also to their rightful owners.

